<p>Once you know which channel you like, go deeper with practical project-based courses on <a href="/udemy/">Udemy</a> (frequently on sale) or <a href="/skillshare/">Skillshare</a> for social content, Canva and video editing. For the thinking behind it all, Seth Godin's [[amazon:book-this-is-mkt|This Is Marketing]] is the best plain-English primer on why people buy.</p>

<p><strong>Core tool stack</strong> (most have free tiers): Google Analytics and Search Console, Canva, CapCut, Meta Business Suite, a scheduler like Buffer or Later, Mailchimp or Kit for email, Google Docs and Sheets for reporting, and an SEO suite like Semrush when clients justify the cost. AI writing and image tools speed up first drafts and research, but clients pay for your judgment, editing and results, not raw AI output.</p>

