<h2 id="90-day-plan">How to start a digital marketing side hustle: a 30/60/90-day plan</h2>
<p>This plan assumes 5–10 hours a week alongside a full-time job.</p>

<h3 id="days-1-30">Days 1–30: Learn and build proof</h3>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><strong>Choose one service and one type of client.</strong> Example: "Instagram management for local restaurants" or "Google Business Profile optimization for home service companies."</li>
  <li><strong>Complete one or two free certifications</strong> from the table above that match your service.</li>
  <li><strong>Practice on yourself.</strong> Grow a test Instagram account, optimize a friend's Google Business Profile, or launch a small blog to learn SEO hands-on.</li>
  <li><strong>Do one free or heavily discounted project</strong> for a local business, nonprofit or friend in exchange for a testimonial and permission to share results.</li>
</ol>

<h3 id="days-31-60">Days 31–60: Package and pitch</h3>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><strong>Turn your project into a one-page case study:</strong> problem, what you did, results (with numbers if possible).</li>
  <li><strong>Create two or three fixed packages</strong> with clear deliverables (see pricing below). Packages are easier to buy than hourly rates.</li>
  <li><strong>Set up a simple presence:</strong> a LinkedIn profile that names your service, a one-page site or Notion portfolio, and optionally a <a href="/fiverr/">Fiverr</a> gig for inbound leads.</li>
  <li><strong>Pitch 5–10 targeted businesses a week</strong> with a specific observation and offer (more on this below).</li>
</ol>

<h3 id="days-61-90">Days 61–90: Deliver and systematize</h3>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><strong>Over-deliver for your first one or two clients.</strong> Send a short monthly report showing what you did and what changed.</li>
  <li><strong>Build templates</strong> for onboarding, content calendars, reports and invoices so each new client takes less setup time.</li>
  <li><strong>Ask for referrals and reviews</strong> at the 60-day mark, when clients are happiest.</li>
  <li><strong>Raise prices for new clients</strong> once you have two or more testimonials.</li>
</ol>

<div class="callout"><strong>Quick tip:</strong> Cap yourself at two or three retainer clients while you still have a day job. Burning out and missing deadlines is the fastest way to lose the referrals that make this side hustle grow.</div>

